From: shaohong.dong <shaohong.dong.cq@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: split the native compiler command for code generation

OpenEmbedded BUILD_CXX can contain trailing whitespace or a compiler wrapper.
Parse it into a CMake command list rather than treating the whole environment
value as an executable filename during cross compilation.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: shaohong.dong <shaohong.dong.cq@gmail.com>
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@ if(CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING)
     # If cross-compiling, assume 'c++' is the host compiler if not specified via HOST_CXX.
     # Users can set HOST_CXX to point to their native compiler.
     if(DEFINED ENV{HOST_CXX})
-        set(HOST_CXX_COMPILER $ENV{HOST_CXX})
+        separate_arguments(HOST_CXX_COMPILER UNIX_COMMAND "$ENV{HOST_CXX}")
     else()
         set(HOST_CXX_COMPILER "c++")
     endif()
